diff — Compare two files or directories line by line.
Usage: diff [OPTION]... FILE1 FILE2
Use - for standard input. Use -- to end option processing.
Normal output lists insertions, deletions and replacements. -u and -c include context.
-y compares columns, -e/-f produce editor commands, -n emits RCS changes, -D NAME merges inputs.
-q reports differences, -s reports equality. -r descends into directories. -N treats missing files as empty.
-i folds case. -E, -Z, -b, -w and -B ignore selected whitespace differences. -I RE ignores matching changes.
Examples: diff -u a b
          diff -qr olddir newdir
          diff --label old --label new -u - file
Status 0 means identical, 1 different and 2 trouble. Comparison requires read access.
Help, version and manual require no file access or temporary storage.

--normal | -q --brief | -s --report-identical-files
    Normal output, summary of differences, or report equality.
-c -C N --context[=N] | -u -U N --unified[=N]
    Context or unified output. Default context is three lines.
-e --ed | -f --forward-ed | -n --rcs | -D --ifdef NAME
    Reverse ed, forward ed, RCS, or conditional compilation.
-y --side-by-side | -W --width=N | --left-column | --suppress-common-lines
    Two columns, width (default 130), common lines on the left or omitted.
-p --show-c-function | -F --show-function-line=RE | -L --label=TEXT
    Mark the enclosing function. Set one or two file labels.
-t --expand-tabs | -T --initial-tab | --tabsize=N | --suppress-blank-empty | -l --paginate
    Expand tabs, align text, set tab stops (default 8), suppress blank prefixes or paginate.
-r --recursive | -N --new-file | -P --unidirectional-new-file | --no-dereference
    Descend into directories, compare absent files as empty on both sides or on the left, compare symlink targets.
-x --exclude=PAT | -X --exclude-from=FILE | -S --starting-file=NAME
    Skip matching names, load one pattern per line, or start at NAME.
--ignore-file-name-case | --no-ignore-file-name-case | --from-file=FILE | --to-file=FILE
    Set case rules for names, or compare each operand to a fixed left or right file.
-i --ignore-case | -E --ignore-tab-expansion | -Z --ignore-trailing-space
    Fold case or ignore tab expansion or trailing whitespace.
-b --ignore-space-change | -w --ignore-all-space | -B --ignore-blank-lines | -I --ignore-matching-lines=RE
    Ignore changes in spacing, all spaces, blank-only changes or groups matching a basic expression.
-a --text | --strip-trailing-cr | --binary
    Treat NUL as text, remove CR before LF, or use byte input.
--line-format=FMT | --{old,new,unchanged}-line-format=FMT | --{old,new,changed,unchanged}-group-format=FMT
    Format lines with %L or %l. Groups use %<, %>, %= and numeric fields. %% prints a percent sign.
-d --minimal | -H --speed-large-files | --horizon-lines=N
    Select minimal edits, accelerate large inputs, or retain N matching boundary lines.
--color[=WHEN] | --palette=PALETTE
    Use never, auto or always. Override colors with entries such as de=31:ad=32.
--help | -v --version
    Display documentation or the component version.
